# Line endings.
#
# Every source text file in this repo stays LF in the working tree on every
# platform, including a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true. This is not a
# style preference: tooling here slices the raw bytes of index.html and looks for
# a literal '\n' (tests/examples.test.js did, and failed on a CRLF checkout even
# on a correct tree). Pinning eol=lf removes that whole class of failure instead
# of making each tool defend against it.
#
# `text=auto` is the baseline: git stores LF in the index for anything it detects
# as text. The explicit rules below also force LF on checkout.

* text=auto

*.html  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.xml   text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf

# Raster images: never touched, never line-ending-converted. A CRLF conversion
# applied to a PNG corrupts it.
*.png   binary
